{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And what remains of it until morning.</b> What does Scripture mean by <b>until morning</b> a second time? To set one morning against another — for 'morning' connotes from the time the sun rises, so Scripture comes to teach that it is forbidden to eat from the rising of dawn. This is according to its plain sense. And there is another midrash: it teaches that it is not burned on the Festival day but on the morrow — and thus you expound it: ״וְהַנּוֹתָר מִמֶּנּוּ בְּבֹקֶר רִאשׁוֹן״ — ״עַד בֹּקֶר שֵׁנִי תַּעֲמֹד וְתִשְׂרְפֶנּוּ״ (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:35.389001523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}